d 'MINDF': module to perform HLT unit root tests with up to three breaks in trend (Harvey, Leybourne and Taylor, 2013)
d
d  mindf computes the minimum Dickey-Fuller unit root tests of
d Harvey, Leybourne and Taylor (2013, Journal of Econometrics)
d allowing for up to three breaks in the linear trend. Trend breaks
d are permitted under both the unit root null and the
d trend-stationary alternative, so the tests remain valid when
d breaks occur in a unit root process. The ADF lag order is
d selected by the MAIC of Ng and Perron (2001) computed on
d OLS-detrended residuals, following Perron and Qu (2007). 
d
d KW: time series
d KW: structural breaks
d KW: unit roots
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260722
d
d Author: Ozan Eruygur,  Ankara Haci Bayram Veli University
d Support: email eruygur@@gmail.com
d
